7.2 Optimize initial application rendering
The initial application interface should become available without waiting for every background operation to finish.
Establish a clear distinction between:
•	Application initialization.
•	Authentication restoration.
•	Critical user data.
•	Page-specific information.
•	Background operations.
Use appropriate loading indicators or skeleton components.
Avoid blank screens caused by waiting for noncritical data.
Do not display protected content before authorization has been established.
7.3 Optimize React rendering
Implement justified improvements to:
•	Expensive components.
•	Repeated rendering.
•	Large data lists.
•	Chart rendering.
•	SVG rendering.
•	State management.
•	Heavy calculations.
Use React performance tools where available.
Avoid introducing unnecessary global state.
7.4 Optimize animation performance
RevOS contains animated and interactive visual components.
Investigate:
•	Scroll-triggered animations.
•	SVG animations.
•	Repeated layout calculations.
•	JavaScript-driven animations.
•	Expensive transitions.
•	Animations running outside the visible viewport.
Prefer transform and opacity animations when suitable.
Use CSS animations where possible.
